Usage: cloudburrow storage-server [flags]

Run CloudBurrow's own Cloud Storage server, built to Google's spec (#485). Methods
not built answer 501 notImplemented.

Flags of storage-server:
  -listen address
    	address to serve on (default 127.0.0.1:4443)
  -host names
    	comma-separated host names clients use, for virtual-hosted XML requests
    	(<bucket>.<host>)
  -allow-remote
    	permit a non-loopback listen address, which exposes an unauthenticated server
  -data-dir directory
    	keep state there, durably (default: memory only)
  -mode persistent|ephemeral
    	persistent (the default) keeps -data-dir across restarts; ephemeral
    	deletes what an earlier run left there before serving
  -signing-cert email=path.pem
    	verify that service account's signed URLs against this public
    	certificate or key (repeatable); any other signed URL is refused
  -cors-allow-origin scheme://host[:port]
    	answer browser requests from this origin as well as loopback ones
    	(repeatable or comma-separated); any other Origin is refused with 403
  -pubsub-emulator host:port
    	deliver notifications to this Pub/Sub emulator; without it,
    	notificationConfigs cannot be created (501)

Flags:
  -allow-remote
    	permit binding a non-loopback address (unsafe)
  -bind-address string
    	IP address to publish host endpoints on
  -cluster-provider string
    	cluster provider (only kind is supported)
  -config string
    	path to a JSON configuration file
  -cors-allow-origin value
    	web origin (scheme://host[:port]) whose browser requests Cloud Storage answers, beyond loopback ones; repeatable or comma-separated (default: loopback origins only)
  -hook-env string
    	comma-separated variables of this environment passed to hooks beyond PATH, HOME, LANG, TMPDIR and the like
  -hook-timeout duration
    	time limit for each hook script (default 5m)
  -hooks-dir string
    	directory of ready.d and shutdown.d hook scripts (default .cloudburrow/hooks)
  -kubeconfig string
    	explicit kubeconfig path (never the developer default)
  -local-ai-alias string
    	comma-separated model IDs that resolve to the configured model (explicit substitution)
  -local-ai-embeddings
    	serve text-embedding :predict for embeddinggemma-300m-onnx-community, a community ONNX conversion that is NOT an official Google artifact (needs a -tags onnx build)
  -local-ai-image string
    	local AI runtime image (default: the image published with this release; for a dev build, the one make litert-lm builds)
  -local-ai-model string
    	host path to a .litertlm model; enables the local generation endpoint
  -local-ai-model-id string
    	model ID clients must request (default: the catalogue entry for the artifact)
  -log-level string
    	log level: trace, debug, info, warn, error
  -mode string
    	state mode: ephemeral or persistent
  -name string
    	instance name; scopes the cluster, namespace and every owned resource
  -namespace string
    	namespace for CloudBurrow-managed workloads
  -node-image string
    	pinned kind node image, which fixes the Kubernetes version
  -port-base int
    	move every fixed default port so the layout starts here (control here, ingress +80, console +90); explicit --port-* flags still win (0 = the defaults, from 9000)
  -port-bigquery int
    	BigQuery emulator REST host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9014)
  -port-bigquery-storage int
    	BigQuery Storage Read API gRPC host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9015)
  -port-bigtable int
    	Bigtable emulator host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9012)
  -port-cloudsql int
    	Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9019)
  -port-cloudsql-mysql int
    	Cloud SQL for MySQL host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9017)
  -port-console int
    	host port for the web console (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-control int
    	control port for health, readiness and admin (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-datastore int
    	Datastore emulator host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9011)
  -port-firestore int
    	Firestore emulator host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9010)
  -port-ingress int
    	host port for the cluster ingress gateway (0 = OS-assigned; fixed at cluster creation)
  -port-kms int
    	Cloud KMS host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9018)
  -port-localai int
    	host port for the local generation endpoint (0 = OS-assigned; requires -local-ai-model)
  -port-logging int
    	Cloud Logging host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9009)
  -port-memorystore int
    	Memorystore (Valkey, RESP) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9016)
  -port-metadata int
    	host port for the local metadata server (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-pubsub int
    	Pub/Sub host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-resourcemanager int
    	Resource Manager v3 Projects API host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9007)
  -port-run int
    	Cloud Run host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-scheduler int
    	Cloud Scheduler host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9008)
  -port-secrets int
    	Secret Manager host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-spanner int
    	Spanner emulator host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9013)
  -port-storage int
    	Cloud Storage host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-tasks int
    	Cloud Tasks host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -project string
    	default project ID (default: the instance name when it is a valid project ID, otherwise derived from it)
  -ready-timeout duration
    	bounded time to wait for cluster components to become ready
  -seed-file string
    	seed document (the /admin/seed body) applied when up starts
  -services string
    	comma-separated services to start (default storage,pubsub,tasks,run,secretmanager; opt-in: firestore,datastore,bigtable,spanner,cloudsql,bigquery,memorystore,cloudsql-mysql,scheduler,logging,kms)
  -shutdown-timeout duration
    	bounded time to drain on shutdown
  -state-dir string
    	host directory for the generated kubeconfig and other artifacts
